        {
          "path": "_m/g/c/6/f/jerpoint-abbey-wp/unfortunately-no-detai.jpg",
          "filename": "Graveslab Jerpoint 1.jpg",
          "caption": "Unfortunately, no details can be found on the Historic Environment Viewer about any of the grave slabs or tombs, but I would presume this is an early one, i.e. 13th/14th century. Carrigan describes the fashion as being Edwardian by which he means the first 3 English kings called Edward.[1] At his time, he was able to read \"HIC IACET THOMAS S [...] P[RO]PICIETUR5 DEUS. A. MC°C°C° PAT. N. AC [AVE]\" which he translates to \"Here lies Thomas S [on whose soul] God have mercy. A.[D.] 1300. Pater noster et [Ave].\"[2]\nGPS is an estimation.",
          "alt": "Unfortunately, no details can be found on the Historic Environment Viewer about any of the grave slabs or tombs, but I would presume this is an early one, i.e. 13th/14th century. Carrigan describes the fashion as being Edwardian by which he means the first 3 English kings called Edward.[1] At his time, he was able to read \"HIC IACET THOMAS S [...] P[RO]PICIETUR5 DEUS. A. MC°C°C° PAT. N. AC [AVE]\" which he translates to \"Here lies Thomas S [on whose soul] God have mercy. A.[D.] 1300. Pater noster et [Ave].\"[2]\nGPS is an estimation.",
          "width": 2016,
          "height": 4032,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
          "artist": "A.-K. D.",
          "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Graveslab_Jerpoint_1.jpg",
